<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="46708ba3">&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Report mock-ups are mostly used for internal reporting or when new reports are being developed.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        For the development of regulatory and compliance reports, mock-ups might not be required as the&lt;br /&gt;
        structures for these reports are mostly finalized and dictated by regulatory agencies.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The reporting platform and user interface should be taken into account while designing mock-ups and any platform
        constraints should also be taken into account.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="758eaaee"></attribute>
<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="828d744b"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="7c576818">The report mock-up design process begins during requirement gathering and requires inputs from all System Development Life
Cycle (SDLC) teams (analysis, development, and testing teams) along with expertise from various systems owners (business
and technical).</attribute>
</Element>
